# Commands and results

- `go test -tags=unit ./internal/service`: passed. Covers strict window-set comparison, full reset, maximum deduction, invalid state rejection, one-time daily handling, expiry protection, and versioned cache invalidation.
- `pnpm exec vitest run src/utils/__tests__/subscriptionQuota.spec.ts src/components/subscription/__tests__/SubscriptionQuotaAdvanceDialog.spec.ts src/views/user/__tests__/SubscriptionsView.spec.ts`: passed 15 tests. Covers the mandatory window list, cancellation, full request payload, state-change error, insufficient validity, and entry visibility.
- `go test -tags=unit ./...`: passed across all backend packages.
- `pnpm --dir frontend run test:run`: passed 219 files and 1643 tests.
- `pnpm --dir frontend run typecheck`: passed.
- `pnpm --dir frontend run lint:check`: passed.
- `pnpm --dir frontend run build`: passed.
- `git diff --check`: passed.

# Skipped checks

- PostgreSQL/Redis integration tests tagged `integration` were not run because the local environment has no Docker CLI (`docker` is not recognized). The concurrent quota-advance integration test was updated to expect `QUOTA_ADVANCE_STATE_CHANGED` for the losing request, but it remains unexecuted locally.

# Spec consistency

- The dialog derives the entire exhausted, advanceable window set and submits that exact set without a client-side deduction value.
- The service recomputes the set after `GetByIDForUpdate`; any mismatch rejects before `Update` with `QUOTA_ADVANCE_STATE_CHANGED`.
- The maximum remaining normal-reset duration is deducted once, all matching windows reset together, and insufficient validity keeps the entry visible while disabling confirmation.
- The change does not modify administrator reset, payment, refund, auto-renewal, receipt, or cache-invalidation architecture.

# Known limitations and risks

- Real PostgreSQL lock contention, receipt replay, and Redis cache behavior were not exercised locally because Docker is unavailable.
- Code review noted pre-existing transaction-boundary and refresh-read concerns in `subscription_quota_advance_receipt.go`; that file is outside this change and was not modified.

# Conclusion

The changed quota-cycle behavior is covered by fresh backend and frontend automated checks, with static review evidence for unchanged compatibility paths and lock-order behavior. The unavailable Docker integration environment is recorded above.
